{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1197111-ananasi-first-rites","id":1197111,"title":"Ananasi First Rites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-19T03:26:17-07:00","id":1197111,"title":"Ananasi First Rites","content":"Old stuff,<br /> <br /> First Rites<br /> Before Ananasi are released into the world, the teachers<br /> that have been brought together to show them the way<br /> of Ananasa take the time to teach them the rites that they<br /> will need to establish themselves as a part of the Great Web.<br /> These are not complicated rites, but they are designed to<br /> grow with the spider as she finds her way on Earth.<br /> <br /> <br /> New stuff,<br /> <br /> Rites<br /> The Ananasi share quite a few rites with the Ovid,<br /> especially Mystic rites. The Ananasi also have a number<br /> of their own rites, taught during their time of Umbral<br /> instruction, or whispered to them by Queen Ananasa<br /> inside of their Sylie. One rite stands above all others in<br /> importance, however.<br /> <br /> So, the Rites background for Ananasi, do they get any rites for free to start with? Like the first rites? And then all the other rites are initially bought with background dots? This has always confused me.<br /> <br /> And adding to this, how does an Ananasi learn a rite if they First Rites are already known? I understand the Triumverate Rites would be learned form the Queen or from another Ananasi, but the First Rites, which every Ananasi was taught to begin with, if they require the dots, then how are they learned if not all of the First Rites are known (and there are more than 5 levels worth of First Rites.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23984,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","user":"Thkaal","date":".  Further questions to be clarified on this topic. 03-19-2018, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T13:37:38-07:00","id":1521835,"title":"","content":"I know it's ancient but....any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T15:14:04-07:00","id":1521839,"title":"","content":"My interpretation is that the First Rites are... the Rituals Knowledge. That covers most of the incidentals of background knowledge that First Rites would theoretically cover.<br /> <br /> Also, congrats on sticking it out on the topic for 5 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T18:20:06-07:00","id":1521844,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that &quot;First Rites&quot; are less of actual Rituals as a mechanic they learn and that they are more a broad education any young spider needs to have. That means dots in Rituals and Occult, rather than actual mechanical Rituals. You use the Rites background for any Rites you would need to learn.<br /> <br /> Also... 5 years. Wow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T02:19:35-07:00","id":1521861,"title":"","content":"The way it is written in the Breed Book seems to imply Ananasi learn the First Rites in spiderling school and would get them for free at character creation. Rite of Spinning is essential, Rite of Appeal and Tapping Ananasa's Wisdom are needed for character advancement. CB20 skips the latter two and implies they are covered by resting in the Sylie, and Ananasa will simply grant Rank and Gifts when she sees it fit.<br /> I prefer the Breed Book version and give the three Rites for free. If the character doesn't have the minimum dots in Rituals, they know the Rites but can't enact them. Any further First Rites can be purchased with the Background or learned later from other Ananasi or Ananasa herself through Tapping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T03:29:07-07:00","id":1521864,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, three free points that go into a narrative tool aren't really important. So it's not like you're doing harm by allowing them to have the basics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}